**Postfix configuration** (`/etc/postfix/main.cf`):
- `myorigin = local.edu` — all outgoing mail uses the local.edu domain
- `transport_maps` — routes list addresses (`reading-group-join@`, `reading-group-leave@`, `reading-group@`, etc.) to Mailman's LMTP on port 8024
- `virtual_mailbox_domains = local.edu` — treats `local.edu` as a virtual domain for user delivery
- `virtual_mailbox_maps` (regexp) — maps `user@local.edu` to `/var/mail/user`
- `default_transport = local` — non-list addresses fall through to local delivery

**Services running**:
- Postfix on port 25 (SMTP)
- Mailman LMTP on port 8024
- Mailman REST API on port 8001

